---
const benchmarks = [
  { metric: "Startup Latency (Cold execution)", interpreter: "1.2ms (Zero compile)", VM: "5.4ms", rustC: "120ms (Compilation block)" },
  { metric: "Fibonacci(35) Arithmetic speed", interpreter: "244ms (AST traversing)", VM: "42ms (Bytecode VM)", rustC: "2.1ms (Nativo AOT)" },
  { metric: "Memory Overhead (Base runtime memory)", interpreter: "1.8MB", VM: "2.4MB", rustC: "450KB" }
];
---

<div class="text-gray-800 leading-relaxed">

  <h1 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-3 tracking-tight">Dryad Programming Language</h1>

  <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
    A multi-paradigm dynamically typed programming language inspired by JavaScript/TypeScript,
    designed for rapid infrastructure automation and ultra-lightweight native binaries. Through
    a unique hybrid execution architecture, Dryad compiles strictly typed code paths directly
    to ARM64/x86_64, while maintaining an instant-on interpreter for sandboxed scripting.
  </p>

  <p class="text-sm mb-8">
    <a href="/docs/introducao-e-filosofia" class="text-emerald-800 no-underline hover:underline font-semibold">Read the Spec →</a>
    <span class="text-gray-300 mx-2">·</span>
    <a href="/docs/tabela-codigos-de-erro" class="text-emerald-800 no-underline hover:underline font-semibold">Error Codes →</a>
  </p>

  <div class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Triple Execution Engine</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-2">
      Instantly switch between a <strong>Tree-Walking Interpreter</strong> for immediate
      scripting, a <strong>Stack-Based Bytecode VM</strong> for reliable intermediate
      performance, and <strong>AOT Native Compilation</strong> with no periodic garbage collector.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm">
      <a href="/docs/modelo-de-execucao" class="text-emerald-800 no-underline hover:underline font-semibold">How the execution pipeline works →</a>
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Deterministic Safety</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-2">
      Predictable memory cleanup via <strong>automatic Reference Counting with no tracing GC</strong>,
      triggered the moment structures go out of scope or threads terminate, with bounds-checking
      support for low-level arrays.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm">
      <a href="/blog" class="text-emerald-800 no-underline hover:underline font-semibold">No-Nonsense Deep Dive on the Blog →</a>
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Quick Start</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-3">
      The official installer detects your CPU architecture (x86_64 or ARM64) and instantly
      sets up the <code class="text-emerald-800 font-semibold">dryad</code> CLI in your PATH:
    </p>
    <pre class="bg-gray-900 text-emerald-400 p-4 text-sm leading-snug overflow-x-auto select-text mb-3 font-mono">$ curl -fsSL https://dryad.dev/install | sh
<span class="text-gray-500 italic"># Installing Dryad Toolkit v1.0.0... Ready.</span>
$ dryad run scripts/main.dy
<span class="text-gray-500 italic"># Hello World! Running dynamically via AST Interpreter.</span>
$ dryad build --aot scripts/main.dy -o output_bin
<span class="text-gray-500 italic"># Converted to IR, optimized with Constant Folding & native ELF output.</span></pre>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Comparative Performance</h2>
    <div class="text-sm leading-relaxed overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-left text-sm border-collapse">
        <thead>
          <tr class="text-gray-500 text-xs border-b border-gray-200">
            <th class="py-1.5 pr-3 font-semibold">Metric</th>
            <th class="py-1.5 px-3 font-semibold">AST Interpreter</th>
            <th class="py-1.5 px-3 font-semibold">Bytecode VM</th>
            <th class="py-1.5 px-3 font-semibold">AOT Native</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {benchmarks.map((bch) => (
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-100">
              <td class="py-1.5 pr-3 text-gray-800">{bch.metric}</td>
              <td class="py-1.5 px-3 text-gray-600">{bch.interpreter}</td>
              <td class="py-1.5 px-3 text-gray-600">{bch.VM}</td>
              <td class="py-1.5 px-3 text-gray-600">{bch.rustC}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2 italic">Benchmarked on Apple M2 ARM64.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-4">
    <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">DESIGN PHILOSOPHY</h2>
    <blockquote class="text-sm text-gray-600 italic leading-relaxed">
      "Clarity over performance: Legibility, syntactic consistency, and clean error messages
      with suggestions are unconditionally prioritized over obscure runtime optimizations."
    </blockquote>
  </div>

</div>
